---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../site';
---

<Base
  title={`Privacy policy — ${site.name}`}
  description={`How ${site.name} handles your account, your messages and your photos.`}
>
  <section class="section legal">
    <div class="wrap legal__inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="h2">Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="legal__updated mono">Applies to Serafim v{site.version} · {site.packageId}</p>

      <p class="lead">
        This is a plain description of what the app does with your data,
        written from the app's actual behaviour. It is short on purpose.
      </p>

      <h2>What we store</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Your account.</strong> The email address you sign in with,
          your display name, username, bio, avatar, and the interests you
          choose. Your email is only used to sign in and to recover access.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Your profile photo.</strong> Stored in a private storage
          bucket that only you can write to, so nobody can overwrite your
          picture.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Your messages.</strong> Text messages, group membership,
          friendships, follows and notifications are stored on Serafim's own
          database so they can be delivered to other people and shown to you
          on your next device.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Your device token.</strong> A push notification token, so
          Serafim can tell your phone about a new message. It is removed when
          you sign out.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Your preferences.</strong> Theme, text size, chat
          backgrounds, read receipts, privacy choices and message retention
          settings, kept on your device.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What we do not store</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Chat photos and voice notes.</strong> These are never
          uploaded to our servers. They are resized on your phone and then
          delivered to the people in the conversation, who keep their own
          copies. If a participant deletes a photo, it is removed from the
          device where it happened.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Your password.</strong> Sign-in is handled by a third-party
          identity service. Your password is sent directly to it and never
          reaches Serafim servers, which only ever see a session token. The
          refresh token is kept in encrypted storage on your device.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Your attention.</strong> There is no advertising SDK and no
          analytics SDK in the app. We do not sell your data, and we do not
          build advertising profiles.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Who else is involved</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Supabase</strong> — sign-in, the primary database and
          private file storage.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Cloudflare</strong> — the edge network that fronts the
          API so the app stays reachable on restrictive mobile networks.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Google</strong> — sign-in, and push delivery for Android
          notifications.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Each of them processes data only to provide the service it is there
        for. None of them receive your chat photos or voice notes, because
        those never reach a server.
      </p>

      <h2>Your controls</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Lock your profile to hide friends, followers and following.</li>
        <li>Turn read receipts on or off.</li>
        <li>Decide whether anyone, only friends, or nobody can add you to groups.</li>
        <li>Choose whether strangers may send you friend requests.</li>
        <li>Set how long messages are kept on your device.</li>
        <li>Delete a message for yourself, or for everyone in the conversation.</li>
        <li>Delete your account and everything attached to it.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        Serafim is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly
        collect information from them.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes, the new version will be published here and
        announced in the official SERAFIM chat inside the app.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions, requests, or corrections:{' '}
        <a href="mailto:hello@serafim.app">hello@serafim.app</a>, or open an
        issue on <a href={site.repo} target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>.
      </p>

      <p class="legal__back">
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/">← Back to the homepage</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal__inner {
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  .legal__updated {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
  }

  .legal :global(h2) {
    margin: 2.5rem 0 0.75rem;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0;
  }

  .legal :global(ul) {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
  }

  .legal :global(li) {
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--text-dim);
  }

  .legal :global(li strong) {
    color: var(--text);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .legal :global(p) {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--text-dim);
  }

  .legal__back {
    margin-top: 3rem;
  }
</style>
